		{"id":"a429b5e9371e33bb","type":"file","file":"ParSys/Theory of Paralelisim/Speed Equasions ParSys.md","x":-829,"y":-2200,"width":449,"height":913},
		{"id":"f692cba6a21c4933","type":"text","text":"# Assignment 5\nT1\n#TODO  Aus Algorithmus den Ex Time & speedup ziehen\nT2\n# Performance Rate $R_i = \\frac{I_{ci}}{T_i}$\n![[Arithmetic mean performance]]\n![[Geometric mean performance]]\n![[Harmonic mean performance]]\nT3\n### MIPS\n$$MIPS = \\frac{f}{CPI \\cdot 10^6}$$\nf = clock rate\nCPI = cycles per Instruction\n### \\# of Instructions\n$$I_c = T \\cdot MIPS \\cdot 10^6$$\n$T$ = Execution Time\n### FLOPS = $\\frac{I_c}{T}$\n### MFLOPS = $\\frac{I_c}{T\\cdot 10^6}$","x":-2840,"y":4940,"width":660,"height":1460},
		{"id":"7fedd3ce4daba93f","type":"text","text":"# Assignment 4\nT1\n### Effective [[Speedup]]\n$S= \\frac{T_{seq}}{T}$, with $\\color{blue}T_{seq} = T \\cdot \\text{\\% of non-paralized} + T \\cdot \\text{\\% of Paralized} \\cdot \\#\\text{Processors}$\n\n### Ratio of vectorized code\n$\\alpha = \\frac{T\\cdot \\%\\text{programm in par} \\cdot \\#\\text{Processors}}{T_{seq}}$\n\nT2\n### Effective [[MIPS-rate]] = $\\frac{W}{T}$\n$\\alpha$ = fractin code that can be parallelized\n$n$ = ampount Processors with execution rate of $x$ MIPS\n$W$ = Workload\n$$T = \\frac{\\alpha \\cdot W}{n \\cdot x} + \\frac{(1-\\alpha)W}{1 \\cdot x}$$ = [[Execution Time]] for Parralell + for sequencial\n\nT3\n### Average Speedup with [[Arithmetic mean performance]]\n\n$\\alpha$ = probability of sequencial\n$0 \\leq a \\leq \\alpha \\leq b \\leq 1$\n$R$ = Execution rate\n$\\color{blue}T(\\alpha) = \\frac{\\alpha}{R} + \\frac{1-\\alpha}{nR}$\n$$T_{Ari} = \\frac{\\int_a^b T(\\alpha) d\\alpha}{b-a} = \\frac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b\\frac{\\alpha}{R} + \\frac{1-\\alpha}{nR} d\\alpha$$\n#### Average Execution rate:\n$$\\color{blue}R_{avg} = \\frac{1}{T_{avg}}$$\n#### Average Speedup:\n$$\\color{blue}S_{avg} = \\frac{R_{avg}}{R}$$\n","x":-3600,"y":4940,"width":660,"height":1580},
